+      "file": "STUCK_FRAMES threshold",
+      "finding": "The stuck detection counter STUCK_FRAMES=180 is now compared against dt60-scaled accumulation. At 60Hz: dt60≈1.0 so 180 frames ≈ 3 seconds trigger. At 144Hz real time-to-trigger changes because dt60 per frame is smaller (144/144*60=actual_ms_ratio), and the stuck detection is correctly real-time-based now. The STUCK_FRAMES constant is a frame count in old code; in new code it is effectively ~180 * (1/60s) of real time, meaning the threshold is the same real-time stuck duration regardless of Hz. However, the visual appearance threshold STUCK_DIST_THRESHOLD is still distance-based so no net change there. This change means display Hz no longer causes early/late stuck detection — a correct fix."
+    },
