 ─  ⚕ Hermes  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
                                                                                
     The JSON output is valid and the Discord post completed. Summary of        
     findings:                                                                  
                                                                                
     Delta-time fix a120267 — Review Summary                                    
                                                                                
     The fix correctly converts frame-rate-dependent physics to                 
     real-elapsed-time-normalized, using dt60 = dt * 60 to scale all            
     per-frame operations to a 60fps baseline regardless of display Hz          
     (144Hz, 60Hz, 30Hz, etc.).                                                 
                                                                                
     Key findings:                                                              
                                                                                
     1. Tests call b.update() with no dt60 argument — 22 call sites in          
     b01_ball_physics.test.js. In the test environment, dt60 is undefined,      
     making gravity/position NaN. At real 60Hz hardware dt60=1.0 so tests       
     mostly pass, but the fundamental assumption that one update() call =       
     one frame is broken.                                                       
                                                                                
     2. STUCK_FRAMES and teleportCooldown — changed from integer frame          
     counters to dt60-scaled real-time values. Stuck detection is now           
     correctly time-based, not Hz-dependent, but tests expecting exactly        
     180 update() calls to trigger will fail on high-Hz displays.               
                                                                                
     3. FRICTION changed from linear to exponential — vx *= FRICTION → vx       
     *= Math.pow(FRICTION, dt60). At dt60=0 (first frame), friction becomes     
     1 (no drag) vs the old 0.995 per-frame. Physically correct at all Hz,      
     but breaks test assertion values.                                          
                                                                                
     4. simulatePreviewArc() now time-based — old 80-frame loop over 1.3s       
     at 60Hz but 0.55s at 144Hz. New1.3-second simulation changes arc           
     landing positions — slot landing tests in b02_drop_mechanics.test.js       
     will see different endpoints.                                              
                                                                                
     5. No variable-refresh-rate test coverage — the suite only runs at         
     whatever host Hz the test browser happens to have. No test                 
     exercises120Hz or 144Hz scenarios.                                         
                                                                                
     6. updateParticles(dt60) — signature changed; any test calling it          
     without dt60 gets NaN life decay.                                          
                                                                                
     Coverage gaps: No test passes explicit dt60 values, no test covers Hz      
     other than 60, no test covers dt=0 first-frame edge case, no test          
     covers dt60 > 1.0 for 120Hz/144Hz+ displays.                               
                                                                                
